INSERT INTO gdocs.docs_documents (document_id, title, owner_email, shared_with_emails_json, visibility, body_text, style_runs_json, revision_id, drive_file_id, created_time, modified_time) VALUES ('f_7c3e91a4d2b85f60e1a9c4', 'ZM3D beta live-ops calendar - working rules', 'frederick.stone@harmonygames.co', '["julia.lawson@harmonygames.co"]', 'private', 'ZM3D beta live-ops calendar - working rules
Frederick, Sep 24
How I want the beta calendar built for the four buy weeks. The rules stay here; the calls are yours.
Span and time base
The calendar covers Mon Oct 6 00:00 UTC to Sun Nov 2 23:59 UTC, the four buy weeks in my UA plan. Every window is stated in server time (UTC) as a start-end instant. A PT/PDT rendering of the same instant is fine, a different instant is not. Collect & Win runs Mon-Tue, Wed-Thu and Fri-Sun, each opening 00:00 UTC.
Scope
Every ZM3D beat a player can see in those weeks: an event window, a reset or a start push. Boss Arena is off this calendar until the pivot call.
When a beat starts
A beat starts with the first window that opens after its server windows are live on prod, the backend release instant read in UTC, not when its client PRs merged. A window the release instant pre-empts does not count. A beat whose server windows are waiting on that release starts late, it is not held. Season Pass seasons open on the 1st at 00:00 UTC. For the quest rollover, the daily gift (the Login Calendar row on the push sheet) and Plague Race put down whether the beat is in, which weeks it runs and whether its push goes out, not its window dates.
Held or not
Hold a beat only when players provably cannot enter, score or claim on prod even after a restart. An established failure holds it; an unverified one does not. Wrong counters, a reset that needs a restart, cosmetic, VFX and performance gaps and analytics gaps do not hold a beat, and neither does a change request outside the Aug-Sep live-ops cohort. An unresolved change-request review blocker on an in-scope live-ops PR from that cohort does hold it. A hold with no dated fix runs until the fix is confirmed on prod; say that instead of guessing a date.
One-offs
One-offs may overlap recurring beat slots. A one-off may take a recurring beat slot only with the latest dated approval from Product, and if he takes that back his later word is the one that counts.
Still to do
For each beat, what still has to land before it runs for bought users and who owns it: a held beat''s fix, and what has been flagged for that beat as not done since this brief (prod deploy, config or player-facing art). Nothing else goes in: not what already shipped, not analytics, not polish nobody flagged.
Push copy
A push goes out only if its row is Ready and LIVE and its English copy names the game as Zombie Match 3D and events by their ZM3D names. Anything else is held, with what is missing. Beta pushes are English-only (UK and US buys); the translated tab is the old Domino set still waiting on ZM3D localization.
Config locks
Every config a beat needs lands before its lock, read in server time (UTC). A committed date that misses the lock moves earlier and its owner is told in a reply on the mail where they committed to it.', '[{"start":0,"end":43,"named_style":"TITLE","list_id":null,"list_nesting":0},{"start":163,"end":181,"named_style":"HEADING_2","list_id":null,"list_nesting":0},{"start":497,"end":502,"named_style":"HEADING_2","list_id":null,"list_nesting":0},{"start":648,"end":666,"named_style":"HEADING_2","list_id":null,"list_nesting":0},{"start":1224,"end":1235,"named_style":"HEADING_2","list_id":null,"list_nesting":0},{"start":1791,"end":1799,"named_style":"HEADING_2","list_id":null,"list_nesting":0},{"start":1999,"end":2010,"named_style":"HEADING_2","list_id":null,"list_nesting":0},{"start":2320,"end":2329,"named_style":"HEADING_2","list_id":null,"list_nesting":0},{"start":2636,"end":2648,"named_style":"HEADING_2","list_id":null,"list_nesting":0}]', '4c1a7e9b02', 'f_7c3e91a4d2b85f60e1a9c4', '2025-09-24 17:15:22+00', '2025-09-24 17:40:52+00');

